ytime_forever": 2037, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 228, "playtime_at_review": 618, "last_played": 1790824609, "avatar": "48da18eafdcab0cfe65f4025aafe8768b1d7c971"}, "language": "english", "review": "I truly enjoy this continuation of the Sniper Elite series! The mechanics of the game are remarkable. The maps are generous for the missions. Plenty of places to explore even while in combat with the enemy. If you played Sniper Elite 3, 4 or 5 you should feel right at home with this game! I recommend it it 100%", "timestamp_created": 1784435116, "timestamp_updated": 1784435116, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1738246187", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "230793530", "author": {"steamid": "76561197983520277", "personaname": "Kampfferkerl", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Kampfferkerl/", "num_games_owned": 675, "num_reviews": 39, "playtime_forever": 1228, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 527, "last_played": 1789335344, "avatar": "3bed8d1a1ba454dc01c1cfade6d79ce58798a9c8"}, "language": "english", "review": "Read a few mixed reviews before purchase and thought: “It’ll be fine.”\n\nNo.\n\nNononononono.\n\nThis is nowhere near Rebellion’s level of refinement.\n\nThese feel like mediocre generic FPS maps on which you’re allowed to play a Sniper Elite game.\nSome even feel like Deathmatch arenas. I just played a mission with over ten Panzerfausts lying around — and not a single tank anywhere — and entire sections of the map are completely empty, while other areas have enemies that aren’t relevant for progression at all.\n\nMost maps are also severely underpopulated. Roughly half the enemy density compared to the last Rebellion title.\n\nFirst map is also the 4th map.\nMost maps have corridor - arena - corridor.\n\nit really shows that Rebellions mechanics are not the mos important aspect of their games, it is their expert mapping skill.\n\nWe also encountered bugs like enemies shooting through walls (Kees got shot through solid cover), enemy snipers who get killed in a kill cam and then STILL return fire, or completely passive enemies who only react if you run straight into their face.\n\nWe’re having fun because we’re playing co‑op, but if I had bought this at full price for single‑player, I’d be very unhappy.\n\nPS: Why does this thing never go on a deep discount.\nPPS: I adore the other Sniper Elite games.", "timestamp_created": 1784415772, "timestamp_updated": 1784416943, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 7, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.550889492034912109", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1738246187", "hardware": {"system_ram": "31830", "os": "Windows 11", "cpu_name": "AMD Ryzen 7 7800X3D 8-Core Processor           ", "adapter_description": "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080", "vram_size": 15977}, "reactions": []}]}